@startuml
title Local-first application package flow

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 18
skinparam BoxPadding 8
skinparam MaxMessageSize 80

actor "Classmate" as User
participant "Classmate laptop\nCodex / AI agent" as Agent
participant "Franklee MCP server\napplication-package-mcp" as MCP

== Setup ==

User -> Agent : Ask for cover letter / CV helper
Agent -> MCP : get_client_skill()
MCP --> Agent : Skill instructions
Agent -> MCP : get_workspace_template()
MCP --> Agent : Folder structure and example files
Agent -> User : Create local workspace

note over Agent
Local workspace contains:
candidate/profile.json
candidate/evidence.md
candidate/tone.md
jobs/<role>/job.md
outputs/<role>/
end note

== Recommended local-first generation ==

User -> Agent : Add CV/profile/job files locally
Agent -> Agent : Read local candidate files
Agent -> Agent : Read local job description
Agent -> MCP : get templates, schemas, rules
MCP --> Agent : LaTeX format contract,\nvalidation checklist,\nwriting rules
Agent -> Agent : Generate cover-letter.tex locally
Agent -> Agent : Compile PDF locally
Agent -> Agent : Check page count and PDF safety
Agent -> Agent : Generate cv-tailored.md locally
Agent --> User : Save files under local outputs/

note over MCP
In this recommended mode,
the MCP server does not read the classmate's files,
does not process private CV data,
and does not run the final PDF tests.
It provides reusable instructions, templates,
schemas, and validation rules.
end note

== Privacy boundary ==

Agent -x MCP : Do not send candidate CV/profile/evidence
Agent -x MCP : Do not ask server to generate PDF
Agent -x MCP : Do not ask server to validate private documents

note over User, MCP
The MCP server is only a distribution layer.
It provides instructions, workspace files,
templates, schemas, and checklists.
All private processing stays on the laptop.
end note

@enduml
